      article.main
        h1 Iteration
        p
          | Pug supports two primary methods of iteration:
          code each
          | and
          code while
          | .
        h2#each
          | each
          a.header-anchor(href="#each" aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p Pug’s first-class iteration syntax makes it easier to iterate over arrays and objects in a template:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive" data-index="0")
          div.row(data-reactroot data-reactid="1" data-react-checksum="-1941202962")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  ul
                    each val in [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
                      li= val
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly data-reactid="7").
                  <ul>
                    <li>1</li>
                    <li>2</li>
                    <li>3</li>
                    <li>4</li>
                    <li>5</li>
                  </ul>
        p You can also get the index as you iterate:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive" data-index="1")
          div.row(data-reactroot data-reactid="1" data-react-checksum="1891541579")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  ul
                    each val, index in ['zero', 'one', 'two']
                      li= index + ': ' + val
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly data-reactid="7").
                  <ul>
                    <li>0: zero</li>
                    <li>1: one</li>
                    <li>2: two</li>
                  </ul>
        p Pug also lets you iterate over the keys in an object:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive" data-index="2")
          div.row(data-reactroot data-reactid="1" data-react-checksum="1004380996")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  ul
                    each val, key in {1: 'one', 2: 'two', 3: 'three'}
                      li= key + ': ' + val
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly data-reactid="7").
                  <ul>
                    <li>1: one</li>
                    <li>2: two</li>
                    <li>3: three</li>
                  </ul>
        p The object or array to iterate over is just plain JavaScript. So, it can be a variable, or the result of a function call, or almost anything else.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive" data-index="3")
          div.row(data-reactroot data-reactid="1" data-react-checksum="-1457612903")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  - var values = [];
                  ul
                    each val in values.length ? values : ['There are no values']
                      li= val
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly data-reactid="7").
                  <ul>
                    <li>There are no values</li>
                  </ul>
        p
          | One can also add an
          code else
          | block that will be executed if the array or object does not contain values to iterate over. The following is equivalent to the example above:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive" data-index="4")
          div.row(data-reactroot data-reactid="1" data-react-checksum="-1711632048")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  - var values = [];
                  ul
                    each val in values
                      li= val
                    else
                      li There are no values
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly data-reactid="7").
                  <ul>
                    <li>There are no values</li>
                  </ul>
        p
          | You can also use
          code for
          | as an alias of
          code each
          | .
        h2#while
          | while
          a.header-anchor(href="#while" aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p
          | You can also use
          code while
          | to create a loop:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive" data-index="5")
          div.row(data-reactroot data-reactid="1" data-react-checksum="881430681")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  - var n = 0;
                  ul
                    while n < 4
                      li= n++
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly data-reactid="7").
                  <ul>
                    <li>0</li>
                    <li>1</li>
                    <li>2</li>
                    <li>3</li>
                  </ul>
        div(style="margin-top: 50px")
